{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod","id":784697,"title":"Mortis Ghost's OFF In The CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-12T06:13:24-08:00","id":784697,"title":"Mortis Ghost's OFF In The CoD","content":"Major spoilers ahead for those who haven't played <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/OFF\" target=\"_blank\"><b>OFF</b></a>. I am also aware that Cthonians are vaguely defined in 1ED, and that they will likely be expanded upon or altered somehow in 2ED.<br /> <br /> To sum it up, the Batter is an inhuman entity that takes on the form of a baseball batter and goes on a quest to &quot;purify&quot; the world. In order to do this, he has to destroy the Guardian of each level (referred to as a Zone), which reduces said level to a featureless white landscape filled with disturbing sounds and monstrous shades. As the story progresses, it is revealed that the Guardians were not always so bad, and that they too had hopes and dreams of building a better world. You are made to question to validity of the Batter's quest, and when you reach the final level, any semblance of righteousness is gone: the Batter doesn't want to fix the world, he wants to annihilate it. At the very end, you can choose to side with the Batter and turn off the switch to end it all, or rebel against him to no avail, leaving behind the purified Zones that may never come back to life.<br /> <br /> It is a surreal and tragic, but very gripping and fascinating game. The creator, Mortis Ghost, does not give any ultimate answers to the meaning of the story, which leaves each player to decide what it means. But I digress.<br /> <br /> Let's suppose someone wants to bring the Batter into an NWOD game. Regardless of which ending is chosen in OFF, the Batter persists in the NWOD as a shade of a world that is no more. Does that qualify him as a Cthonian, or is there some other type of monster he could be? In OFF, he destroys godlike entities and legions of specters on his own, so I believe he's Rank 5. I already have a Ban for him, but what could be the Bane of a genocidal abomination who disguises itself as a holy crusader?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-03-2016, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T15:17:40-08:00","id":785015,"title":"","content":"The Chicago Cubs? Why not take out a godlike baseball themed abomination with a team that is notorious for having not truely &quot;won&quot; in over 100 years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:59:46-08:00","id":787035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=785015#post785015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chicago Cubs? Why not take out a godlike baseball themed abomination with a team that is notorious for having not truely &quot;won&quot; in over 100 years?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know any baseball trivia, so your joke flew over my head. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Let me rephrase: what is symbolically/thematically fitting as the Bane of an entity who only thinks in black-and-white terms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:10:26-08:00","id":787110,"title":"","content":"Anything Grey, really. A murder weapon used by a saint (metaphorically speaking). A monster's symbol of redemption. Anything the proves there are no simple &quot;heroes&quot; and &quot;villains&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T02:51:47-08:00","id":787245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=787035#post787035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know any baseball trivia, so your joke flew over my head. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Let me rephrase: what is symbolically/thematically fitting as the Bane of an entity who only thinks in black-and-white terms?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=787110#post787110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything Grey, really. A murder weapon used by a saint (metaphorically speaking). A monster's symbol of redemption. Anything the proves there are no simple &quot;heroes&quot; and &quot;villains&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll parrot this, anything that shows the world to be morally gray and not easily defined as Black and White/Good and Evil. Batter thinks he is a Hero, but his true form is that of a Demonic Duck maybe one of his powers is also an illusion that hides his true form and makes him appear as a &quot;Batter&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also possible he's a Sin-Eater himself... YOU the player are his Geist and when you leave him in one of the endings it leaves him capable to Die permanently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 12-16-2015, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:52:01-07:00","id":905634,"title":"","content":"Wow this post is a little old, so I hope I'm not doing a disservice by posting in it, but, I'd sooner portray the Batter is a goetia from Mage books than a Cthnonian, but I like Rickman's idea that he's one of the Bound and at complete odds with his giest--which one's the annihilator and which one is the Puppeteer capable of retracting their desire to see the Batter's goal's fulfilled, I am not sure.<br /> <br /> As a goetia, I guess I should explain that its because I adhere to the theory that the game OFF <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> take's place in Hugo's mind and the Batter is causing Hugo brain-death by destroying the last visages of his hope, leaving the only things remaining, the Secretaries the only thing remaining, as they represent what's killing Hugo to begin with and got him sick. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 06-02-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:44:05-07:00","id":905821,"title":"","content":"All I know is, if the batter is ephemeral, he should have Smoke, Metal, Plastic, and Meat as Influences. Maybe <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sugar, but that might also make a good Bane.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Also, what about the onion rings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:46:46-07:00","id":906724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=905821#post905821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is, if the batter is ephemeral, he should have Smoke, Metal, Plastic, and Meat as Influences. Maybe <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sugar, but that might also make a good Bane.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Also, what about the onion rings?</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume you mean the Add-Ons? I frankly don't know what they would be.<br /> <br /> Since the day I started this thread, I've discussed OFF with some users via private message, and one of the interpretations was a Slasher. At first, this didn't make sense to me, since Mortis Ghost confirmed that the Batter is not a human being. But then I remembered that Scourges weren't 100% human either. And that's when it clicked. The Batter could be a Legend. His entire mission is about righting a perceived wrong, no matter the cost. He can always come back, as long as the story/Player behind him keeps going.<br /> <br /> To me, that is the scariest part about the Batter. He is just a puppet, for some reason or another. And puppets can only act if there is something or someone pulling the strings. How much of what we saw was what it seemed to be? Is the puppeteer justified? Could the tragedy have been avoided? Who's to blame?<br /> <br /> I can see why these questions would be especially pertinent to the Slasher interpretation, as they are arguably the most human monsters.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't know how that would be translated into an actual session. In OFF, the Batter cannot be defeated. An invincible antagonist is tricky for tabletop. If I include a way to stop him, does that take away from the horror and make the whole idea of using him pointless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-03-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:00:40-07:00","id":906812,"title":"","content":"To understand the Batter and his mission we need to take a look at the metaphysics of the game. We are dealing with a deeply unnatural environment that can ultimately be torn down. It should be relatively easy to place him in someone's Oneiros, Abyssal Verge, Time Splinter or other strange realm. On the other hand using him in the Material Realm requires additional considerations. Making him a mere killer would do the character a disservice. Having him adapt to a new world would require some character development, which doesn't seem like something Batter is capable of. Keeping him an existential threat would make him a Tier 4 villain or at least a threat to everything the characters know. It can be done, however. An unrelenting killer destroying God-Machine Infrastructures could cause damage on a global scale. Giving him a mission to destroy the Underworld or the Hisil could also be appropriate. To scale down we could make him a threat to a single characters life - and I mean totality of the victims experience, not just their life functions. A bit like for Hugo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:49:37-07:00","id":906845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=906812#post906812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To understand the Batter and his mission we need to take a look at the metaphysics of the game. We are dealing with a deeply unnatural environment that can ultimately be torn down. It should be relatively easy to place him in someone's Oneiros, Abyssal Verge, Time Splinter or other strange realm. On the other hand using him in the Material Realm requires additional considerations. Making him a mere killer would do the character a disservice. Having him adapt to a new world would require some character development, which doesn't seem like something Batter is capable of. Keeping him an existential threat would make him a Tier 4 villain or at least a threat to everything the characters know. It can be done, however. An unrelenting killer destroying God-Machine Infrastructures could cause damage on a global scale. Giving him a mission to destroy the Underworld or the Hisil could also be appropriate. To scale down we could make him a threat to a single characters life - and I mean totality of the victims experience, not just their life functions. A bit like for Hugo.</div> </div> </div> </div> Scourges aren't mere killers, but you made some good points. Let's see...<br /> <br /> If he's destroying Infrastructure, he should be capable of perceiving it. The options we have for that are Angels, Demons, Stigmatics, Offspring, Nephilim and Cryptids. Out of these, Angel seems the most appropriate, but there's obviously something broken about his mission. His sportive outfit and weapon of choice might have been caused by a filing error somewhere in the Infrastructure that built him. It's likely that he was supposed to be a Destroyer, but his programming was corrupted somehow, turning him into an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/246019-primer-corrupted-programs-aberrations-of-the-god-machine\"><b>Aberrant</b></a>. If we take into account Numina, Manifestations, Influences, Incepts, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities\"><b>&quot;Angelic Form&quot;</b></a> and Linchpins, he certainly counts as an existential threat. I'd say he's Rank 3. I'm hard pressed to imagine how a Stigmatic could represent the same threat.<br /> <br /> As for making him a threat to a single character above all else...he can still do that as an Angel (or Qashmal). Perhaps an Abyssal?<br /> <br /> I also considered a Huntsman version with &quot;purity&quot; as their Tell. That would certainly make him relentless and merciless, but he'd be an existential threat of a different sort. His powers would change as well. The baseball bat and outfit would probably be a random memory of the escaped changeling that found its way into the animating ritual. I'd like to point out that the Batter might not have a true form, and neither do the Huntsmen. The humanoid form of this Huntsman!Batter would be just one among many. It would be harder to use this version outside of a Changeling game, though.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:41:52-07:00","id":906876,"title":"","content":"The idea of him being in someone's Oneiros would fit with the theory Scarlet Witch presented (which was also my interpretation). Maybe he's a Beast. &quot;Purification&quot; could be a valid expression of a Hunger, couldn't it? I haven't read Beast yet.<br /> <br /> Also, since this topic is kind of drifting away from Geist, I can move the thread to the General CofD forum and/or change the title if folks want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:31:35-07:00","id":906903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=906876#post906876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of him being in someone's Oneiros would fit with the theory Scarlet Witch presented (which was also my interpretation). Maybe he's a Beast. &quot;Purification&quot; could be a valid expression of a Hunger, couldn't it? I haven't read Beast yet.<br /> <br /> Also, since this topic is kind of drifting away from Geist, I can move the thread to the General CofD forum and/or change the title if folks want.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for moving and renaming the thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think the Batter is closer to a Hero if we're using Beast terms. He has the same demented faith in the righteousness of his cause. And the change in his appearance during the Judge's ending is not a literal transformation, but a symbolic representation of how the Player and the Judge now see him as an abomination.<br /> <br /> It just occurred to me that he could also be a Banisher who acquired the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\"><b>Abyssal Arcanum</b></a>. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T02:00:49-07:00","id":907036,"title":"","content":"I favor any option that doesn't make him a person. I feel he doesn't just have faith in the mission. For him there is nothing but the mission. A particularly focused Angel or Abyssal do fit the bill. I could also see him as Fetch-spawn, something Lower or a Man in Black v2. He could be a Slasher and I didn't want to imply that they are mere killers. I just think that after what Batter did most Scourges pale in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:17:40-07:00","id":910572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784697-mortis-ghost-s-off-in-the-cod?p=907036#post907036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I favor any option that doesn't make him a person. I feel he doesn't just have faith in the mission. For him there is nothing but the mission. A particularly focused Angel or Abyssal do fit the bill. I could also see him as Fetch-spawn, something Lower or a Man in Black v2. He could be a Slasher and I didn't want to imply that they are mere killers. I just think that after what Batter did most Scourges pale in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. Whether or not he is saddened by what he has to do is very much up to the player's interpretation. I have seen a ton of fanart where is crying and mourning, though. <br /> <br /> I feel like the nature of the world in OFF is relevant in this discussion. I can easily see it as a Splinter timeline, as described in Demon. I think the Guardians of the Zones are more like mutated Stigmatics than Angels. Their power comes from the Queen, who does seem like a high Rank Angel. <br /> <br /> But what about Zacharie? His behavior is very suspicious, and the way he teleports brings Embeds/Manifestations to mind. His friendship with the Judge and Valerie, the book about the Toad King and the statue in the amusement park only add to the mystery. His nonchalant attitude is similar to how someone might feel about playing a minor role in a world that is only technically real. Perhaps he's an Angel who knows he is on the way to Falling and leaving that Splinter? And what is his relationship to Sucre? He doesn't laugh when you tell him that Sucre died. Sucre can apparently see the Batter for what he really is, so she might be a Stigmatic, with her implied addiction being her Stigmata. Mortis said that both Zacharie and Sucre are humans, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-09-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}